
######## Friday, the 6th of September, 1940 (mild (11° to 21°C)) ########
   ✦ The run begins in 1940: everybody is 9 years older than in January 1931.
   ✦ The papers of the years before: 30 days remembered.
   ✦ Mr. Thomas retires; Mr. Hale is chief clerk.
   ⚑ Arthur: In the summer of 1934 Joan, at eleven, won a place at the central school; she would stay at school till she is fifteen, and learn shorthand and book-keeping, while a girl who leaves at fourteen brings home ten shillings a week. Did Arthur let Joan take it? → YES (3:0) He lets her take it, because he thinks it will be good for her to earn money.
   ✎ Joan was offered a central-school place in 1934; Arthur let her take it.
   ✎ Joan left school in July 1938: an apprentice to a dressmaker, 5s. 0d. a week.
   ♥ Bert began walking out in February 1933 with Mary Jones, who works at the tin-box works in Southwark.
   ♥ Bert and Mary Jones were married on Saturday, the 23rd of December, 1933.
   ⚑ Ada: Bert and Mary Jones were to be married on Saturday, the 23rd of December, 1933, and they had no rooms of their own. Rooms in the Buildings are seven or eight shillings a week. Does Ada have them to live with her in her two rooms after the wedding, till they can find rooms of their own? → YES (3:0) She has them to live with her, because she is fond of Bert and Mary, and because she does not wish to be separated from them.
   ♥ Bert and Mary Jones are married; they live with Ada.
   ✿ Mrs. Edith Hale has had a baby girl.
   ◆ Ada's past: He has never been known to gamble.
   ◆ Arthur's past: He was always particular about paying his bills punctually, and never ran into debt.
   ◆ Mr. Thomas's past: He was punctual and methodical in all his proceedings, and never allowed himself to fall into arrear.
   📅 Ada means to: Monday: washes up the breakfast things, and cleans Bert's boots
   📅 Arthur means to: Monday: pays the household bills, make out the list of provisions for the week, and sees the baby
   ✠ The black-out: no light may show after dark.
   ✠ England is at war with Germany.
   ✠ Rationing begins: bacon, butter and sugar.
   ✠ Bert Turner registers, and is reserved.
   ✠ young Mr. Fenn is called up for the Army.
   ★ Arthur has run into debt.
