--- Mrs. Ada Turner's diary, Sunday, the 8th of September, 1940 (0/5 key facts kept) ---
I stayed in my rooms, listening to the sirens, and thankful to be alive and under a roof.

--- Mr. Arthur Hale's diary, Sunday, the 8th of September, 1940 (0/2 key facts kept) ---
To-day young Mr. Fenn has been called up and gone into the Army.

--- Mr. Walter Thomas's diary, Sunday, the 8th of September, 1940 (0/0 key facts kept) ---
Sunday, September 8, 1940. To-day I have been thinking of my boy in the Army, and of England at war.
